      "message": "this *might* be hardcoding little-endianness, which deserves at least a comment.\n\nalternatively maybe this needs to be byte swapped and wrapped in a htons()\n\nhowever... the key thing about a u16 is it makes the logic easier\n\nThe first 2 bytes of an ipv6 header are (in network order)\n\nWWWWXXXXXXYYZZZZ\n\nW is the version \u00276\u0027\nX is the dscp field\nY is the ecn field\nZ is the first 4 bits of the flowlabel\n\n(with u32 this is a little easier to think of since you then have the full 20 bit flow label field)\n\nsomething like:\n\nread 2 bytes in network order, v \u003d read_u16(offset)\nconvert to host order, v \u003d ntohs(v)\nmask out appropriate 6 dscp bits: ie. v \u0026\u003d 0xF03F\nor in 6 dscp bits: ie. v |\u003d (new_dscp \u003c\u003c 6)\nconvert to network order, v \u003d htons(v)\nstore 2 bytes in network order, write_u16(offset, v)",
